s its source_index. Stage2Admission holds those two vectors, admitted and deferred. An empty candidate list returns both vectors empty, and an unknown strategy throws. The pose node calls it with its detection_selection strategy and a count of one, so stage 2 still estimates that single admitted pallet. The admitted source index and the deferred source indices are written on PalletPoseStamped after input_depth_stamp. The message already carries this pair's RGB and depth stamps, so the split is this capture while the scene can still change. When the estimate fails, publish no PalletPoseStamped and write the same two lists on the failure diagnostic, which is the only result that path publishes. The two early returns that publish nothing stay as they are. The user named which detections are sent through stage 2 versus marked deferred. The part they did not name is that the split is these two admission vectors, ordered by that first-maximum rule, on the pose result the handling process reads.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"message_fields\": [\n    \"pps_perception_msgs/msg/PalletPoseStamped.msg:header\",\n    \"pps_perception_msgs/msg/PalletPoseStamped.msg:pose\",\n    \"pps_perception_msgs/msg/PalletPoseStamped.msg:yaw_rad\",\n    \"pps_perception_msgs/msg/PalletPoseStamped.msg:face_normal_rgb\",\n    \"pps_perception_msgs/msg/PalletPoseStamped.msg:plane_inlier_ratio\",\n    \"pps_perception_msgs/msg/PalletPoseStamped.msg:n_face_points\",\n    \"pps_perception_msgs/msg/PalletPoseStamped.msg:chamfer_cost_m\",\n    \"pps_perception_msgs/msg/PalletPoseStamped.msg:accepted\",","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":124,"fileSize":24691,"path":"C:\\Users\\alanpeng\\Desktop\\Self-envolve_agent\\AbsoluteV1.0\\runs\\Absolute_2026-09-28_02\\run.json","readRange":{"startLine":1,"endLine":40},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-aa630187-a201-4a5c-8344-59db51ed4bf6-36\nfc_b2484d38-cb18-98b2-ac1f-d18a6140dfd2_0","st